# Stack conventions

- **Framework**: Next.js App Router (src/), TypeScript strict
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (`src/components/ui`)
- **Data**: Supabase project `cezwtrsleuubrfmbhosn` (Auth, Postgres, Storage) + Drizzle ORM
- **Client data**: TanStack Query for server-state fetching/mutations
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod
- **i18n**: next-intl with `en`, `fr`, and `es` under `src/app/[locale]`

## Visual system (token-based)
- Source of truth: `src/styles/tokens.css` (CSS) + `src/lib/design-tokens.ts` (TS/email)
- Primitives: Graphite, Indigo, Emerald, Amber (product palette)
- Semantic: `--brand` (graphite-900 `#111827`), `--action` (indigo `#6366F1`), `--action-foreground` (white), `--success` (emerald), `--warning`/`--highlight` (amber), canvas `#F9FAFB` / surface white
- Prefer semantic utilities (`bg-action`, `text-brand`, `bg-canvas`) over hex or primitive classes
- Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans (headings), Inter (body); radius 12px; elevation via `--shadow-elevated`
- No IRCC/MIFI government red/blue motifs or official icons

## Domain model
- `organizations` — one tenant per consulting firm (SaaS customer).
- `profiles` + `organization_members` — staff users (Supabase Auth: email/password or Google). For now every member can access all org data. Each profile has optional `rep_*` columns for IMM 5476 (per-account representative).
- `people` — lifelong immigration clients (identity + history)
- `immigration_projects` — time-bound engagements (program_family + jurisdiction + status). `representative_user_id` points at the staff profile whose `rep_*` details fill IMM 5476.
- `project_participants` — people linked to a project with roles; soft-unlink via `left_at`
- `project_forms` — IRCC forms on a project to-do (seeded by program; IMM 5476 always included)
- `project_form_answers` — ask-once questionnaire answers (jsonb) per project
- `form_share_links` — hashed client tokens, 30-day expiry; regenerate without losing answers
- `customer_portal_access` — portal access_code + access_token on a person; passwords in `private.customer_portal_secrets`
- Portal login verification is **server-only** via `verify_customer_portal_login` (service_role). Never call from the browser.
- Client form fill via `/[locale]/fill/[token]` uses service role after token hash lookup.
- `booking_settings` + `booking_availability_rules` — firm timezone, booking window (X days ahead), recurring weekly open hours.
- `booking_services` — bookable consultation types (title, description, duration, price).
- `booking_appointments` — public bookings; guest PII org-DEK encrypted. Public page `/[locale]/book/[token]` uses service role after token hash lookup.
- `booking_blocked_times` — one-off blocked days/ranges on the firm calendar.

## Layout
- `src/app/[locale]/(marketing)` — public pages (landing lives at `[locale]/page` until moved)
- `src/app/[locale]/(app)` — authenticated CRM dashboard: left sidebar + main content (home, projects, people, calendar, services)
- `src/app/[locale]/portal` — customer portal (link + password)
- `src/lib/supabase` — browser/server/middleware clients
- `src/db` — Drizzle schema and DB client
- `messages/` — locale JSON dictionaries

## Product context
Canadian immigration consultant CRM (Yuzu Immigration / Yuzu Solutions). Prefer bilingual UX and firm multi-tenancy with RLS. Primary create flow is one-screen **New project** with inline people.
